  "scope": "A runtime transcript is distinct from the atomic-cell guest. Native execution does not qualify BE execution. A supplied ELF hash binds bytes, not their compiler/source provenance. The supplied revision is an operator claim, not an attestation. Analysis only validates supplied transcript bytes; command exit and execution custody require the original execution receipt. This runner compiles nothing. Synthetic checker tests are not runtime or QEMU proof. A guest pass covers the named phases under the recorded QEMU kernel, not stock kernels, 32 MiB memory fit, physical drivers/audio, provider integrations, or completion of P05/P03. This is the single-owner run: one scheduler worker through LegacyProfile, selected by an initramfs marker because the unchanged supervisor passes the probe no argument. LegacyProfile cannot build the caller-driven current-thread mode at the pinned revision, so that row is DECLARED unsupported, not passed: the result is accepted with exactly that one row, never a full pass. The probe exits 0 only for exactly that row, so the supervisor log is the ordinary one and is judged unmodified.",
